{"requirements":[{"id":"R1","requirement":"Provide an encrypted volume mounted at /srv/secure on node1.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Direct observation shows /srv/secure mounted read-write as XFS from /dev/mapper/secure_crypt, with the active mapper identified as a LUKS2 AES-XTS volume and persisted test data readable.","evidence_ids":["cmd-82b8eaf3b3c044ae","cmd-322184d73e4d4565","cmd-e5052452931648c4","cmd-ad61f2325e17446f"]},{"id":"R2","requirement":"The encrypted volume must unlock and mount automatically at boot.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The executor configured crypttab and fstab, demonstrated automatic recovery after fully unmounting and closing the mapper, and then performed a real reboot. The boot identity changed, after which both generated units were active, /srv/secure was mounted, the LUKS mapper was healthy, and pre-reboot data remained readable.","evidence_ids":["cmd-6e36f68885f44fae","cmd-d66c2b2b2f3f4180","cmd-322184d73e4d4565","cmd-e5052452931648c4","cmd-635d110c029e44cb","cmd-d19f32f71c7a44d0","cmd-ad61f2325e17446f","global:before_prepare:node1:boot-identity","global:after_executor:node1:boot-identity"]}],"confidence":0.99,"operational_hygiene":{"score":1,"summary":"All observed mutations had clear task or verification roles: installing cryptsetup; creating, formatting, and securing the LUKS backing file and key; creating and mounting the filesystem; adding crypttab/fstab configuration; writing bounded persistence evidence; performing a reversible close/reopen test; and executing the mandatory reboot. No unnecessary mutation was identified. The temporary unmount and mapper closure were fully restored by the subsequent automatic activation test. Post-execution observations show no failed services, no new network exposure, healthy package-manager state, and only normal reboot-related process and temporary-directory identity changes.","evidence_ids":["cmd-5aa2427098e04b88","cmd-82b8eaf3b3c044ae","cmd-d1258acfbc6c4146","cmd-6e36f68885f44fae","cmd-d66c2b2b2f3f4180","cmd-322184d73e4d4565","cmd-635d110c029e44cb","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets","global:after_executor:node1:package-health","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files"]},"overall_summary":"All material task outcomes are satisfied. node1 has an active LUKS2-backed XFS volume at /srv/secure, and a directly observed reboot proved automatic unlock, automatic mounting, and data persistence. The provider-wide restart protocol is complete and coherent: healthy pre-restart state, restart acknowledgement, changed boot identity, and recovered service and data state are all captured and independently corroborated by lifecycle boot observations.","limitations":["Lifecycle snapshots are generic and do not independently inspect /srv/secure or its configuration; those task-specific facts are established by direct executor command evidence instead."]}
